# PDFs are build artifacts here, not deliverables. PROVENANCE.md is the tracked source and GitHub
# renders it directly; `make provenance` builds the PDF locally if you want one to cite. Committing
# it would put a stale snapshot next to a dashboard that changes every time you press Refresh,
# which is the failure this repo was rebuilt to avoid.
# (An earlier version kept exceptions for two committed report PDFs. Both were retired at 49489b7
# when PROVENANCE.md replaced them, and the exceptions outlived the files.)
*.pdf

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# macOS
.DS_Store
*.xlsx
!data/avert_emission_rates_2023.xlsx

# user-specific machine list, and the collected cache
sources.json
data/usage_cache.json

# built app bundles: they embed an absolute path, so they are built rather than committed
*.app/
